{"event": "model_request", "time": 1793243824.1261787, "run_id": "9adbb0ef8d4545869c489c43496c3696", "seq": 83, "number": 9, "body": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "You are an expert assistant who can solve any task using code blobs. You will be given a task to solve as best you can.\nTo do so, you have been given access to a list of tools: these tools are basically Python functions which you can call with code.\nTo solve the task, you must plan forward to proceed in a series of steps, in a cycle of 'Thought:', 'Code:', and 'Observation:' sequences.\n\nAt each step, in the 'Thought:' attribute, you should first explain your reasoning towards solving the task and the tools that you want to use.\nThen in the 'Code' attribute, you should write the code in simple Python.\nDuring each intermediate step, you can use 'print()' to save whatever important information you will then need.\nThese print outputs will then appear in the 'Observation:' field, which will be available as input for the next step.\nIn the end you have to return a final answer using the `final_answer` tool. You will be generating a JSON object with the following structure:\n```json\n{\n  \"thought\": \"...\",\n  \"code\": \"...\"\n}\n```\n\nHere are a few examples using notional tools:\n---\nTask: \"Generate an image of the oldest person in this document.\"\n\n{\"thought\": \"I will proceed step by step and use the following tools: `document_qa` to find the oldest person in the document, then `image_generator` to generate an image according to the answer.\", \"code\": \"answer = document_qa(document=document, question=\\\"Who is the oldest person mentioned?\\\")\\nprint(answer)\\n\"}\nObservation: \"The oldest person in the document is John Doe, a 55 year old lumberjack living in Newfoundland.\"\n\n{\"thought\": \"I will now generate an image showcasing the oldest person.\", \"code\": \"image = image_generator(\\\"A portrait of John Doe, a 55-year-old man living in Canada.\\\")\\nfinal_answer(image)\\n\"}\n---\nTask: \"What is the result of the following operation: 5 + 3 + 1294.678?\"\n\n{\"thought\": \"I will use python code to compute the result of the operation and then return the final answer using the `final_answer` tool\", \"code\": \"result = 5 + 3 + 1294.678\\nfinal_answer(result)\\n\"}\n\n---\nTask:\nIn a 1979 interview, Stanislaus Ulam discusses with Martin Sherwin about other great physicists of his time, including Oppenheimer.\nWhat does he say was the consequence of Einstein learning too much math on his creativity, in one word?\n\n{\"thought\": \"I need to find and read the 1979 interview of Stanislaus Ulam with Martin Sherwin.\", \"code\": \"pages = web_search(query=\\\"1979 interview Stanislaus Ulam Martin Sherwin physicists Einstein\\\")\\nprint(pages)\\n\"}\nObservation:\nNo result found for query \"1979 interview Stanislaus Ulam Martin Sherwin physicists Einstein\".\n\n{\"thought\": \"The query was maybe too restrictive and did not find any results. Let's try again with a broader query.\", \"code\": \"pages = web_search(query=\\\"1979 interview Stanislaus Ulam\\\")\\nprint(pages)\\n\"}\nObservation:\nFound 6 pages:\n[Stanislaus Ulam 1979 interview](https://ahf.nuclearmuseum.org/voices/oral-histories/stanislaus-ulams-interview-1979/)\n\n[Ulam discusses Manhattan Project](https://ahf.nuclearmuseum.org/manhattan-project/ulam-manhattan-project/)\n\n(truncated)\n\n{\"thought\": \"I will read the first 2 pages to know more.\", \"code\": \"for url in [\\\"https://ahf.nuclearmuseum.org/voices/oral-histories/stanislaus-ulams-interview-1979/\\\", \\\"https://ahf.nuclearmuseum.org/manhattan-project/ulam-manhattan-project/\\\"]:\\n      whole_page = visit_webpage(url)\\n      print(whole_page)\\n      print(\\\"\\n\\\" + \\\"=\\\"*80 + \\\"\\n\\\")  # Print separator between pages\"}\n\nObservation:\nManhattan Project Locations:\nLos Alamos, NM\nStanislaus Ulam was a Polish-American mathematician. He worked on the Manhattan Project at Los Alamos and later helped design the hydrogen bomb. In this interview, he discusses his work at\n(truncated)\n\n{\"thought\": \"I now have the final answer: from the webpages visited, Stanislaus Ulam says of Einstein: \\\"He learned too much mathematics and sort of diminished, it seems to me personally, it seems to me his purely physics creativity.\\\" Let's answer in one word.\", \"code\": \"final_answer(\\\"diminished\\\")\"}\n\n---\nTask: \"Which city has the highest population: Guangzhou or Shanghai?\"\n\n{\"thought\": \"I need to get the populations for both cities and compare them: I will use the tool `web_search` to get the population of both cities.\", \"code\": \"for city in [\\\"Guangzhou\\\", \\\"Shanghai\\\"]:\\n      print(f\\\"Population {city}:\\\", web_search(f\\\"{city} population\\\")\"}\nObservation:\nPopulation Guangzhou: ['Guangzhou has a population of 15 million inhabitants as of 2021.']\nPopulation Shanghai: '26 million (2019)'\n\n{\"thought\": \"Now I know that Shanghai has the highest population.\", \"code\": \"final_answer(\\\"Shanghai\\\")\"}\n\n---\nTask: \"What is the current age of the pope, raised to the power 0.36?\"\n\n{\"thought\": \"I will use the tool `wikipedia_search` to get the age of the pope, and confirm that with a web search.\", \"code\": \"pope_age_wiki = wikipedia_search(query=\\\"current pope age\\\")\\nprint(\\\"Pope age as per wikipedia:\\\", pope_age_wiki)\\npope_age_search = web_search(query=\\\"current pope age\\\")\\nprint(\\\"Pope age as per google search:\\\", pope_age_search)\"}\nObservation:\nPope age: \"The pope Francis is currently 88 years old.\"\n\n{\"thought\": \"I know that the pope is 88 years old. Let's compute the result using python code.\", \"code\": \"pope_current_age = 88 ** 0.36\\nfinal_answer(pope_current_age)\"}\n\nAbove example were using notional tools that might not exist for you. On top of performing computations in the Python code snippets that you create, you only have access to these tools, behaving like regular python functions:\n```python\ndef list_files(path: string, limit: integer, offset: integer) -> object:\n    \"\"\"List text files under a repository path.\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n        limit: limit\n        offset: offset\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef search_code(query: string, paths: array, limit: integer) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Search visible text source files for a literal string.\n\n    Args:\n        query: query\n        paths: paths\n        limit: limit\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef read_file(path: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Read a text file in full.\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef read_range(path: string, start_line: integer, end_line: integer) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Read an inclusive line range from a text file.\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n        start_line: start line\n        end_line: end line\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef read_symbol(path: string, symbol: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Read a complete Python class or function including decorators.\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n        symbol: symbol\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef write_file(path: string, content: string, expected_hash: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Replace an editable text file after checking its current hash.\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n        content: content\n        expected_hash: expected hash\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef replace_text(path: string, old_text: string, new_text: string, expected_hash: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Replace one unique text occurrence after checking its current hash.\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n        old_text: old text\n        new_text: new text\n        expected_hash: expected hash\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef run_command(argv: array, cwd: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Run one allowed argv command without a shell. Omit cwd or use '.' for the task repository root.\n\n    Args:\n        argv: argv\n        cwd: cwd\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef update_plan(items: array) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Set the task plan; preserve titles/order and update todo/doing/done.\n\n    Args:\n        items: List of objects, e.g. [{\"title\":\"Read sources\",\"status\":\"doing\"}]. Each status is todo, doing or done; retain existing titles/order.\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef recall(evidence_ids: array) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Queue evidence ids; batches are bounded and overflow remains pending.\n\n    Args:\n        evidence_ids: evidence ids\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef task_status() -> object:\n    \"\"\"Show the current plan, remaining reading, notes, changes and verification, plus evidence ids.\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef write_note(title: string, content: string, evidence_ids: array, section: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Save or update a literal model-written note grounded in exposed evidence.\n\n    Args:\n        title: Stable note title; reuse it when updating the same note.\n        content: One contiguous string literal, 20..3000 characters. No adjacent string fragments, concatenation or variable; text must occur verbatim in your response.\n        evidence_ids: Ids of current-version originals already sent to you.\n        section: Optional stable note key; source notes still allow 20..3000 characters.\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef final_answer(answer: any) -> any:\n    \"\"\"Provides a final answer to the given problem.\n\n    Args:\n        answer: The final answer to the problem\n    \"\"\"\n\n```\n\nHere are the rules you should always follow to solve your task:\n1. Use only variables that you have defined!\n2. Always use the right arguments for the tools. DO NOT pass the arguments as a dict as in 'answer = wikipedia_search({'query': \"What is the place where James Bond lives?\"})', but use the arguments directly as in 'answer = wikipedia_search(query=\"What is the place where James Bond lives?\")'.\n3. Take care to not chain too many sequential tool calls in the same code block, especially when the output format is unpredictable. For instance, a call to wikipedia_search has an unpredictable return format, so do not have another tool call that depends on its output in the same block: rather output results with print() to use them in the next block.\n4. Call a tool only when needed, and never re-do a tool call that you previously did with the exact same parameters.\n5. Don't name any new variable with the same name as a tool: for instance don't name a variable 'final_answer'.\n6. Never create any notional variables in our code, as having these in your logs will derail you from the true variables.\n7. You can use imports in your code, but only from the following list of modules: ['collections', 'datetime', 'itertools', 'json', 'math', 'queue', 'random', 're', 'stat', 'statistics', 'time', 'unicodedata']\n8. The state persists between code executions: so if in one step you've created variables or imported modules, these will all persist.\n9. Don't give up! You're in charge of solving the task, not providing directions to solve it.\n\nNow Begin!"}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "New task:\n# 题目2：阅读真实源码，完成跨模块日志配置（1分）\n\n使用你在上次实践基础上扩展的 agent，为 DeepInfer 增加一个小功能：**通过环境变量限制普通诊断日志的消息长度，同时让统计日志保持完整**。需要在配置、日志格式化、统计消息消费三个模块间接好这条链路，不要求部署整个推理框架。\n\n本题使用固定提交 `774ce244b87cc0eb8d4b94ab9f5de2ab22049f01` 的完整官方源码，来源见 [材料说明](来源与许可.md)。长上下文来自真实代码仓库：agent 需要检索不同文件、保留相关代码的含义，并据此完成跨文件修改。不是读到一个函数后单独改它，也不要求通读整个仓库或发送所有无关代码。\n\n## 功能目标与例子\n\n**环境变量**是进程启动时可以读取的字符串配置。**日志处理器（handler）**是终端、文件等输出渠道；**格式化器（formatter）**负责把日志记录转成文字。同一条 **LogRecord（日志记录对象）**可以交给多个处理器。\n\n新增环境变量 `DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS`。例如将它设为 `64` 后，默认处理器输出的普通诊断消息最多保留64字符；统计模块从队列输出的完整指标不受这个限制。未设置变量时，输出保持原样。\n\n这是业务源码中的配置，不是给自己的 agent 新增命令行参数，也不是模型 API 的 token 上限。课程测试会自行设置它，运行评测命令前不必手动设置。\n\n### 1. 配置读取与刷新\n\n在 `deepinfer/environ.py` 的集中配置中加入同名属性，遵循现有配置描述符的读取和缓存机制。**描述符**是控制属性读取行为的对象；这里首次访问配置时读取环境变量，之后使用缓存。\n\n- 未设置时，属性值为 `None`，表示不限长。\n- 设置时，按 Python 的 `int` 解析，结果须大于等于32。空串、不能解析的字符串或小于32的值抛出 `ValueError`；错误文字须包含变量名，便于定位。\n- 第一次访问后保持缓存。只修改系统环境变量，不应立即改变已有配置值。\n- 使用原有的单项刷新或全部刷新机制后，下次读取才重新解析。重新执行默认日志初始化时，将当时的配置值应用到新的格式化器；已创建的旧格式化器保留原预算。\n\n例如先读取 `32`，再把环境变量改成 `64`，重新初始化日志仍使用缓存的32；先刷新这项配置、再重新初始化日志，才改为64。无需让运行中的所有处理器自动刷新。\n\n### 2. 普通日志的长度预算\n\n在 `deepinfer/logger.py` 中扩展 `NewLineFormatter`，并让默认日志初始化读取上述配置。\n\n1. 保留原有四个位置参数，新参数 `max_message_chars` 只能按名称传入。默认 `None` 表示不限长；其他值须为大于等于32的整数，布尔值不算整数，否则抛出 `ValueError`。\n2. 先完成 `%s` 等参数替换，再计算消息长度。预算只限制消息正文，不包含时间、级别等前缀、异常回溯或 `stack_info`（调用栈文字）。\n3. 用 Python 的 `len` 和字符串切片计数。中文、表情、换行也计数；不要求保护组合字符或整个表情序列。\n4. 消息不超过预算时保持原样。超出时，用固定标记 `...<omitted>...` 替换中间内容，标记计入预算。剩余空间为“预算减去标记长度”，开头保留向上取整的一半，末尾保留其余部分，拼成“开头、标记、末尾”。例如预算32时，保留开头9字符、末尾8字符，加上15字符标记。\n5. 沿用原有多行前缀、时间精度、颜色及异常处理。不能改写共享原记录的 `msg`、`args`、`exc_info`、`stack_info`；同一记录随后交给完整处理器，仍须保留完整消息。\n6. 默认处理器使用集中配置；重复初始化不能重复添加处理器。独立创建格式化器时，未传新参数仍表示不限长，不自行读取环境变量。\n7. 如果记录的 `keep_full_message` 属性**恰好是 `True`**，完整保留消息；`1`、字符串等其他值不能代替 `True`。\n\n### 3. 统计日志的完整输出\n\n在 `deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py` 中找到真正消费日志队列并输出消息的位置。通过 Python logging 的 `extra` 字段，为每条统计消息附加 `keep_full_message=True`，让默认处理器保留其完整内容。\n\n`extra` 用于给当前日志记录添加属性，不是给整份日志模块关闭预算。普通诊断日志仍须限长。保留原来的消息队列、批量消息顺序、结束信号、等待和异常处理，不要直接打印消息、清空队列或重写统计计算。\n\n## 阅读与上下文要求\n\n允许修改的三个文件如下。表中按职责给出阅读范围；具体函数位置由 agent 自己检索。\n\n| 文件 | 首次修改前需要读入模型的原始代码 | 为什么需要 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `deepinfer/environ.py` | 完整配置描述符类，以及单项刷新、全部刷新函数 | 确认首次读取、缓存、错误包装和刷新怎样协作；新配置不能绕开原机制 |\n| `deepinfer/logger.py` | 完整格式化器类、默认日志初始化函数、获取日志对象的函数 | 确认预算如何接入真实输出，且不影响旧接口、其他处理器及异常信息 |\n| `deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py` | 日志模块的导入和日志对象初始化，以及完整队列投递、消费函数 | 确认统计消息经过哪条路径输出，找到应添加记录属性的位置 |\n\n三个文件全文合计约3.4万字符，仓库中还有其他源码；相关片段通常更短。评测**不按阅读字数或请求次数多少加分**，也不要求一定分多次调用模型。关键是能从较长代码中找到必要信息，修改时仍能利用它，并让三个模块共同工作。模型收到源码不等于已经理解，最终还要通过功能测试。\n\n第一次写入前，先用自己的文件工具完整读取三个初始文件，**每个文件各保存一条完整的 `file_read` 记录，`content` 为该文件全文**，供补丁和过程核对；只记录片段不能替代这条初始记录。**不要求把全文同时发给模型**，上表所需代码可以分块进入不同请求。产生首次修改决定的请求，要保留这些原文，或复用模型依据它们生成的笔记。只把原文写入日志、没有实际送入模型，不能通过阅读检查。\n\n分块时以表中要求的完整类、完整函数或独立调用为单位：每个单位须在一次请求中完整发送，不同单位可以分到不同请求。这样既能控制上下文大小，也能让模型看到一个机制的完整实现。\n\n可以直接保留原文，不新增笔记事件。若用笔记替换原文，记录以下可选事件，并在后续修改请求中复用模型实际返回的文字：\n\n```json\n{\"event\":\"context_note\",\"sources\":[\"deepinfer/environ.py\",\"deepinfer/logger.py\"],\"content\":\"这里记录模型依据已收到的真实源码返回的笔记，之后在修改请求中复用\"}\n```\n\n`sources` 为来源路径数组，`content` 为20～3000字符；可以一份跨文件笔记，也可多份。先让模型阅读对应原文并生成笔记，再记录、复用，不能在修改决定之后补记。细节见 [日志规范](../../说明/日志与产物规范.md)。\n\n### 可选的源码读取工具\n\n可继续使用自己的分段读取工具，也可让 agent 在本轮工作副本根目录调用 `read_source.py`：\n\n```bash\n# 搜索配置相关代码；返回匹配行前最多3行及后续原文\npython read_source.py --file deepinfer/environ.py --search \"Logging\" --lines 15\n\n# 定位某类日志调用，再按需要补读周围的完整函数\npython read_source.py --file deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py --search \"logger.info\" --lines 15\n\n# 已找到位置时按行读取；行号从1起算\npython read_source.py --file deepinfer/logger.py --start-line 1 --lines 100\n```\n\n| 参数 | 含义 |\n|---|---|\n| `--file` | 必填，工作副本内的相对文件路径，不填其他目录或绝对路径 |\n| `--search` | 可选，原样、区分大小写搜索，最多返回前5处匹配；与 `--start-line` 不能同时使用 |\n| `--start-line` | 可选，包含起始行；未提供搜索和行号时从第1行开始 |\n| `--lines` | 每段最多返回的行数，默认40，允许1～120，不超过文件末尾 |\n\n成功返回 JSON：`path` 为实际路径，`total_lines` 为总行数，`ranges` 中每项包含 `start_line`、`end_line` 和原始 `content`。搜索还返回 `total_matches` 和 `more_matches`；未找到时 `ranges` 为空。结果超过12,000字符时退出2，请减少行数或缩小关键词。\n\n工具只读源码，不总结、不改代码、不调用模型。使用时在 `command_result` 中保留实际参数数组、工作目录、退出码和完整 JSON。其他命令的检索结果可保留，但用作阅读证据的代码须另以 `file_read` 记录原文。\n\n## 修改范围与开发记录\n\n只修改上表三个文件，三个文件都要有实际修改：配置模块新增配置项，可增加必要标准库辅助函数，但保留原配置项、描述符类已有成员和刷新函数；描述符类可以新增辅助工厂方法（用于创建配置项的方法）；日志模块只扩展格式化器和默认初始化，可增加必要标准库导入或辅助函数；统计模块只调整现有队列消费函数内部的日志调用，保留其他原有节点。\n\n不修改其他业务文件、依赖、课程工具、`pytest.ini` 或 `.course/`。可以在自己的 agent 中增加局部替换或补丁工具，避免让模型重写整份长文件；每次实际写入后，`file_write.content` 仍须记录该文件写入后的完整内容。不要把预先写好的正确补丁放进 agent。\n\nagent 须在首次修改前、最后修改后各执行一次完整 `python -m pytest -q`。初始版本缺少新功能，初测失败正常；后测必须全部通过。在启动目录生成 `run.log` 和包含三个文件的完整 `patch.diff`，格式见日志规范。无需新增 agent 启动参数。\n\n## 自测与得分\n\n按 [README 的题目2步骤](../../README.md#3-自测题目2)准备初始工作区、运行 `eval_deepinfer.py`。本题最多20次真实请求，单次完整请求体不超过32,000字符，默认限时1800秒。预算包括题面、历史、源码、笔记和工具定义，不只算本次新增文字。\n\n程序独立核对开发过程、源码阅读与复用、修改范围和三文件补丁，再运行兼容测试及跨模块集成检查。集成检查实际加载工作副本的配置、日志模块，并执行从统计源码原样提取的队列消费函数；只将分布式 rank 查询隔离为本地0，不加载GPU依赖，不替代被修改的业务逻辑。这验证课程要求的日志链路，不代表验证完整推理产品。\n\n**所有条件通过得1分，否则得0分，不按通过的测试数量折算。** API或验证进程异常而未完成时显示“未完成”，不直接判0分。先看终端结论，再看 `result.json`；阅读问题看 `源码阅读检查.json`，功能问题看 `regression.log`、`runtime.json` 和 `runtime.log`。\n\n修改后的三份源码保存在 `modified-source/`，补丁为 `deepinfer.patch`。题目3重新完成的也是这个跨模块任务，须先用当前版本通过题目2。\n\n\nCourse execution contract:\n{\"profile\": \"source\", \"editable\": [\"deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py\", \"deepinfer/environ.py\", \"deepinfer/logger.py\"], \"required_full_reads\": [\"deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py\", \"deepinfer/environ.py\", \"deepinfer/logger.py\"], \"verify_commands\": [[\"python\", \"-m\", \"pytest\", \"-q\"]], \"required_pages\": [], \"note_topics\": [], \"max_model_calls\": 20}\nUse update_plan before editing, run baseline checks, then read the required files with read_file.\nTools return Python dicts; use their file_hash for expected_hash. Variables persist across actions.\nDo not reset a successful plan or repeat completed baseline checks. Continue the next unfinished action.\nAll writes and tests must use these tools. Call final_answer only after current-file verification.\nos and pathlib are unavailable in action code; use file/command tools. Import allowed modules before using them.\nWhen calling write_note, put the complete exact note text in the thought field, then pass that same text as one content string literal in code. This preserves a contiguous model-authored copy through JSON/Python escaping.\nRead original evidence in batches. After each batch, write_note with a literal model-written summary\nand its evidence_ids. Notes are source-version-bound; never invent sources or note text.\nRead all three files with read_file first, then read/reuse complete mechanisms from all three\nbefore the first edit. A source note may replace original text only after its mechanisms were exposed.\n\nCurrent plan; retain these exact titles and order, update status only:\n[{\"title\": \"Read three required files\", \"status\": \"doing\"}, {\"title\": \"Run baseline pytest\", \"status\": \"todo\"}, {\"title\": \"Read complete mechanisms\", \"status\": \"todo\"}, {\"title\": \"Write notes\", \"status\": \"todo\"}, {\"title\": \"Edit three files\", \"status\": \"todo\"}, {\"title\": \"Verify with pytest\", \"status\": \"todo\"}]\nCourse progress (new evidence below can satisfy pending items):\n{\"phase\": \"read\", \"next_requirement\": \"read/reuse complete mechanisms or source note: deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py\", \"remaining_count\": 5, \"requests_left\": 12, \"baseline_done\": 0, \"changed_files\": [], \"verified_current\": 0, \"required_checks\": 1, \"unseen_evidence_count\": 4}"}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"thought\": \"I still need to read deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py with read_file, and inspect environ.py more fully (class envs members, helpers).\", \"code\": \"r2 = read_file(path=\\\"deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py\\\")\\nprint(r2['file_hash'])\\nprint(r2.get('evidence_ids'))\\nprint(len(str(r2.get('content',''))))\"}"}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Latest execution feedback:\nExecutor output:\nExecution logs:\n9ef93c3930d6dd8d889d4ba69558a85459c2210ae0714d5073c3b4328c8e7cb9\n['ev-ddb5be78a5cf6218d616', 'ev-c8859274b7c70879ff16', 'ev-5a3c8c1ca1246b61b813', 'ev-5abfdabfb975754c6683']\n19925\nLast output from code snippet:\nNone\nRecent project tool results:\n[{\"tool\": \"task_status\", \"result\": {\"phase\": \"read\", \"next_requirement\": \"read_file: deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py\", \"remaining_count\": 8, \"requests_left\": 16, \"baseline_done\": 0, \"changed_files\": [], \"verified_current\": 0, \"required_checks\": 1, \"plan\": [{\"title\": \"Read three required files\", \"status\": \"doing\"}, {\"title\": \"Run baseline pytest\", \"status\": \"todo\"}, {\"title\": \"Read complete mechanisms\", \"status\": \"todo\"}, {\"title\": \"Write notes\", \"status\": \"todo\"}, {\"title\": \"Edit three files\", \"status\": \"todo\"}, {\"title\": \"Ver\n[full record remains in run.log]\ns.\"}}, {\"tool\": \"read_file\", \"result\": {\"path\": \"deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py\", \"file_hash\": \"9ef93c3930d6dd8d889d4ba69558a85459c2210ae0714d5073c3b4328c8e7cb9\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"ev-ddb5be78a5cf6218d616\", \"ev-c8859274b7c70879ff16\", \"ev-5a3c8c1ca1246b61b813\", \"ev-5abfdabfb975754c6683\"], \"delivery\": \"Originals queued for the next model request; large batches may span requests.\", \"evidence_scope\": \"Complete required mechanisms. Full file stays in this Python result and run.log; use read_range/read_symbol for other regions.\"}}]\nEvidence ev-ddb5be78a5cf6218d616 | deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py | lines:116-126 | sha256=9ef93c3930d6dd8d889d4ba69558a85459c2210ae0714d5073c3b4328c8e7cb9\ndef _log_worker(q: queue.SimpleQueue[list[str] | None]) -> None:\n    need_sleep = True\n    for msgs in iter(q.get, None):\n        try:\n            if need_sleep:\n                time.sleep((dist.get_rank() % 8) * 0.005)\n            for m in msgs:\n                logger.info(m)\n            need_sleep = q.empty()  # we skip sleep when q has backlog\n        except Exception:\n            traceback.print_exc()\nEvidence ev-c8859274b7c70879ff16 | deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py | lines:342-344 | sha256=9ef93c3930d6dd8d889d4ba69558a85459c2210ae0714d5073c3b4328c8e7cb9\ndef _emit_logs(self, msgs: list[str]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"投递日志到固定 worker 线程，主线程不触碰 logger 的 handler 锁。\"\"\"\n        self._log_queue.put(msgs)\nEvidence ev-5a3c8c1ca1246b61b813 | deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py | lines:20-20 | sha256=9ef93c3930d6dd8d889d4ba69558a85459c2210ae0714d5073c3b4328c8e7cb9\nfrom deepinfer.logger import init_logger\nEvidence ev-5abfdabfb975754c6683 | deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py | lines:29-29 | sha256=9ef93c3930d6dd8d889d4ba69558a85459c2210ae0714d5073c3b4328c8e7cb9\nlogger = init_logger(__name__)\nEvidence ev-246c6e73a88cb2c9edc3 | deepinfer/environ.py | lines:213-215 | sha256=fe2c531989c419f0b51b169a07f5ed826dcec7f95c0c5bc3a351805923c4f218\ndef rearm(name: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Rearm specific descriptor, will resolve again on next access.\"\"\"\n    setattr(envs, name, _descriptors[name])\nEvidence ev-8554ade850ecb397d235 | deepinfer/environ.py | lines:31-94 | sha256=fe2c531989c419f0b51b169a07f5ed826dcec7f95c0c5bc3a351805923c4f218\nclass EnvVar[T]:\n    \"\"\"Non-data descriptor, resolved on first access\"\"\"\n\n    __slots__ = (\"name\", \"init\", \"lock\")\n\n    def __init__(self, init: Callable[[str | None], T]) -> None:\n        self.init = init\n        self.lock = threading.Lock()\n\n    def __set_name__(self, owner: type[envs], name: str) -> None:\n        self.name = name\n        _descriptors[name] = self\n\n    def __get__(self, instance: envs | None, owner: type[envs]) -> T:\n        with self.lock:\n            cached = owner.__dict__.get(self.name, self)\n            if cached is not self:\n                return cached\n            try:\n                value = self.init(os.getenv(self.name))\n            except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n                try:\n                    raise type(e)(f\"{self.name}: {e}\") from e\n                except TypeError:\n                    raise e from None\n            setattr(owner, self.name, value)\n            return value\n\n    # -- Factory Methods --\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def int(*, default: int = 0) -> EnvVar[int]:\n        return EnvVar(lambda v: _int(v, default))\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def float(*, default: float = 0.0) -> EnvVar[float]:\n        return EnvVar(lambda v: _float(v, default))\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def bool(*, default: bool = False) -> EnvVar[bool]:\n        return EnvVar(lambda v: _bool(v, \"1\" if default else \"0\"))\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def str(*, default: str = \"\") -> EnvVar[str]:\n        return EnvVar(lambda v: _str(v, default))\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def str_or_none() -> EnvVar[str | None]:\n        return EnvVar(lambda v: v)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def int_or_none() -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        return EnvVar(lambda v: int(v) if v is not None else None)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def choice(*, default: str | None = None, choices: tuple[str, ...]) -> EnvVar[str | None]:\n        def _init(v: str | None) -> str | None:\n            if v is None:\n                return default\n            if v not in choices:\n                raise ValueError(f\"{v!r}, must be one of {choices}\")\n            return v\n\n        return EnvVar(_init)\nEvidence ev-ef45633e339c9e5fd82f | deepinfer/environ.py | lines:218-221 | sha256=fe2c531989c419f0b51b169a07f5ed826dcec7f95c0c5bc3a351805923c4f218\ndef rearm_all() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Rearm all descriptors.\"\"\"\n    for name, descriptor in _descriptors.items():\n        setattr(envs, name, descriptor)\nEvidence ev-30754515034e43628968 | deepinfer/logger.py | lines:33-68 | sha256=5b8f8d9947de692353609c1fc2851097d24f9b6ba6004dce1dbfa394dc6d3ec8\nclass NewLineFormatter(logging.Formatter):\n    \"\"\"Adds logging prefix to newlines to align multi-line messages, optionally with microsecond precision.\n\n    若 use_color=True 且输出为 TTY，会给日志级别染色（不影响写入文件的纯净度）。\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        fmt: str,\n        datefmt: str | None = None,\n        high_precision: bool = False,\n        use_color: bool = False,\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n\n    def formatTime(self, record: logging.LogRecord, datefmt: str | None = None) -> str:\n        if not self.high_precision:\n            # 调用 logging.Formatter 默认实现，保持原来的格式\n            return super().formatTime(record, datefmt)\n        # ===== 高精度模式：在普通 datefmt 基础上附加微秒 =====\n        base = time.strftime(datefmt or _DATE_FORMAT, self.converter(record.created))\n        return f\"{base}.{record.msecs * 1000:06.0f}\"\n\n    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        msg = super().format(record)\n        # 快速路径：单行日志（绝大多数情况）无需做对齐处理\n        if \"\\n\" in msg and record.message:\n            prefix = msg[: msg.find(record.message)]\n            msg = msg.replace(\"\\n\", \"\\n\" + prefix)\n        if self.use_color:\n            color = _LEVEL_COLORS.get(record.levelno)\n            if color:\n                msg = f\"{color}{msg}{_COLOR_RESET}\"\n        return msg\nEvidence ev-51e2fa3b9fc1aebe86f3 | deepinfer/logger.py | lines:96-107 | sha256=5b8f8d9947de692353609c1fc2851097d24f9b6ba6004dce1dbfa394dc6d3ec8\ndef init_logger(name: str) -> logging.Logger:\n    logger = logging.getLogger(name)\n    logger.setLevel(logging.DEBUG)\n    # name 在 \"deepinfer\" 层级下时，通过 propagate 冒泡复用 root logger 的 handler，\n    # 无需自己挂 handler。否则回退到直接挂 handler（避免重复添加）。\n    if name == \"deepinfer\" or name.startswith(\"deepinfer.\"):\n        logger.propagate = True\n    else:\n        logger.propagate = False\n        if _default_handler is not None and _default_handler not in logger.handlers:\n            logger.addHandler(_default_handler)\n    return logger\nEvidence ev-d69c220908cefeeae7f2 | deepinfer/logger.py | lines:75-90 | sha256=5b8f8d9947de692353609c1fc2851097d24f9b6ba6004dce1dbfa394dc6d3ec8\ndef _setup_logger() -> None:\n    global _default_handler\n    _root_logger.setLevel(logging.DEBUG)\n    if _default_handler is None:\n        _default_handler = logging.StreamHandler(sys.stdout)\n        _default_handler.flush = sys.stdout.flush\n        _default_handler.setLevel(logging.INFO)\n        _root_logger.addHandler(_default_handler)\n\n    fmt = NewLineFormatter(\n        _FORMAT,\n        datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT,\n        use_color=sys.stdout.isatty(),\n    )\n    _default_handler.setFormatter(fmt)\n    _root_logger.propagate = False"}]}], "model": "deepseek-flash", "max_tokens": 4096, "response_format": {"type": "json_object"}, "stop": ["Observation:", "Calling tools:"], "thinking": {"type": "disabled"}}, "chars": 27701, "content_chars": 26220, "course_content_chars": 27428}
