me, _descriptors[name]). rearm_all() loops _descriptors. To add DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS with >=32 validation and non-bool, add a factory method returning EnvVar with a lambda that raises ValueError containing variable name.\nModel-authored note logger_stats, sources=['deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py', 'deepinfer/logger.py']:\nlogger.py: NewLineFormatter.__init__(fmt, datefmt=None, high_precision=False, use_color=False) stores flags. format() calls super().format(record) producing full string with prefix and message; then adds prefix after newlines (record.message), applies color. To add budget: add keyword-only max_message_chars after 4 positional params, validate >=32 and not bool, save budget. In format(), truncate record.message portion before multi-line handling - must not mutate record.msg/args. _setup_logger creates handler once, always resets formatter with NewLineFormatter(_FORMAT, datefmt, use_color) - add max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS there. init_logger attaches _default_handler if not already present. stats_logger._log_worker iterates queue batches, calls logger.info(m) per message; change to logger.info(m, extra={'keep_full_message': True})."}]}], "model": "deepseek-flash", "max_tokens": 4096, "response_format": {"type": "json_object"}, "stop": ["Observation:", "Calling tools:"], "thinking": {"type": "disabled"}}, "chars": 23204, "content_chars": 21922, "course_content_chars": 22931}
