et__ checks owner.__dict__ for a cached value, else calls init(os.getenv(self.name)), wraps errors as f'{self.name}: {e}', and setattr caches result. Factory methods are staticmethods returning EnvVar(lambda v: ...). int_or_none returns int(v) if v is not None else None (no validation). rearm(name) does setattr(envs, name, _descriptors[name]). rearm_all() loops _descriptors. To add DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS with >=32 validation and non-bool, add a factory method returning EnvVar with a lambda that raises ValueError containing variable name.\nModel-authored note logger_stats, sources=['deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py', 'deepinfer/logger.py']:\nlogger.py: NewLineFormatter.__init__(fmt, datefmt=None, high_precision=False, use_color=False) stores flags. format() calls super().format(record) producing full string with prefix and message; then adds prefix after newlines (record.message), applies color. To add budget: add keyword-only max_message_chars after 4 positional params, validate >=32 and not bool, save budget. In format(), truncate record.message portion before multi-line handling - must not mutate record.msg/args. _setup_logger creates handler once, always resets formatter with NewLineFormatter(_FORMAT, datefmt, use_color) - add max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS there. init_logger attaches _default_handler if not already present. stats_logger._log_worker iterates queue batches, calls logger.info(m) per message; change to logger.info(m, extra={'keep_full_message': True})."}]}], "model": "deepseek-flash", "max_tokens": 4096, "response_format": {"type": "json_object"}, "stop": ["Observation:", "Calling tools:"], "thinking": {"type": "disabled"}}, "chars": 23526, "content_chars": 22167, "course_content_chars": 23253}
{"event": "model_response", "time": 1793243852.2452896, "run_id": "9adbb0ef8d4545869c489c43496c3696", "seq": 134, "number": 14, "response": {"id": "fdcf75f4-2eee-4df3-877c-2e9224906475", "object": "chat.completion", "created": 1793243849, "model": "deepseek-flash", "choices": [{"index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\"thought\": \"Baseline failed as expected (50 failed, 10 passed). Now edit the three files. Let me first re-read the exact current contents of relevant regions to craft precise replacements.\", \"code\": \"e = read_file(\\\"deepinfer/environ.py\\\")\\nl = read_file(\\\"deepinfer/logger.py\\\")\\ns = read_file(\\\"deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py\\\")\\nprint(e['file_hash'], l['file_hash'], s['file_hash'])\\nprint('=== ENVIRON TAIL ===')\\nprint(e['content'][-1500:])\"}\n\n<additional_data>\n[additional_data]\n{\"plan\": \"[{\\\"title\\\": \\\"Read three required files\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"done\\\"}, {\\\"title\\\": \\\"Run baseline pytest\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"doing\\\"}, {\\\"title\\\": \\\"Read complete mechanisms\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"done\\\"}, {\\\"title\\\": \\\"Write notes\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"done\\\"}, {\\\"title\\\": \\\"Edit three files\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"todo\\\"}, {\\\"title\\\": \\\"Verify with pytest\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"todo\\\"}]\"}\n</additional_data>\n\n<additional_data>\n[additional_data]\n{\"progress\": {\"phase\": \"edit\", \"next_requirement\": \"remaining source changes: deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py, deepinfer/environ.py, deepinfer/logger.py\", \"remaining_count\": 3, \"requests_left\": 7, \"baseline_done\": 1, \"changed_files\": [], \"verified_current\": 0, \"required_checks\": 1, \"unseen_evidence_count\": 0}}\n</additional_data>"}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 6876, "completion_tokens": 355, "total_tokens": 7231, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 5248}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 5248, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 1628}, "system_f