 [{"type": "text", "text": "Model-authored note logger_stats, sources=['deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py', 'deepinfer/logger.py']:\nlogger.py: NewLineFormatter.__init__(fmt, datefmt=None, high_precision=False, use_color=False) stores flags. format() calls super().format(record) producing full string with prefix and message; then adds prefix after newlines (record.message), applies color. To add budget: add keyword-only max_message_chars after 4 positional params, validate >=32 and not bool, save budget. In format(), truncate record.message portion before multi-line handling - must not mutate record.msg/args. _setup_logger creates handler once, always resets formatter with NewLineFormatter(_FORMAT, datefmt, use_color) - add max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS there. init_logger attaches _default_handler if not already present. stats_logger._log_worker iterates queue batches, calls logger.info(m) per message; change to logger.info(m, extra={'keep_full_message': True})."}], "tool_calls": null, "raw": null, "token_usage": null}], "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_17", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "python_interpreter", "arguments": "fmt = read_symbol(path=\"deepinfer/logger.py\", symbol=\"NewLineFormatter\")\nprint(fmt['content'])\nprint('HASH', read_file(path='deepinfer/logger.py')['file_hash'])\nsetup = read_symbol(path=\"deepinfer/logger.py\", symbol=\"_setup_logger\")\nprint(setup['content'])\nprint(read_symbol(path='deepinfer/logger.py', symbol='init_logger')['content'])"}}], "error": null, "model_output_message": {"role": "assistant", "content": {"thought": "eval_est.py already patched. Now logger.py. I need to see the exact NewLineFormatter code and _setup_logger to craft replace_text. Let me read those symbols.", "code": "fmt = read_symbol(path=\"deepinfer/logger.py\", symbol=\"NewLineFormatter\")\nprint(fmt['content'])\nprint('HASH', read_file(path='deepinfer/logger.py')['file_hash'])\nsetup = read_symbol(path=\"deepinfer/logger.py\", sy