'chars': 891, 'exposed': True}], 'notes': {'environ': {'id': 'environ', 'content': \"environ.py: EnvVar is a non-data descriptor with __slots__ and a lock; __get__ checks owner.__dict__ for a cached value, else calls init(os.getenv(self.name)), wraps errors as f'{self.name}: {e}', and setattr caches result. Factory methods are staticmethods returning EnvVar(lambda v: ...). int_or_none returns int(v) if v is not None else None (no validation). rearm(name) does setattr(envs, name, _descriptors[name]). rearm_all() loops _descriptors. To add DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS with >=32 validation and non-bool, add a factory method returning EnvVar with a lambda that raises ValueError containing variable name.\", 'sources': ['deepinfer/environ.py'], 'evidence_ids': ['ev-246c6e73a88cb2c9edc3', 'ev-8554ade850ecb397d235', 'ev-ef45633e339c9e5fd82f'], 'valid': False, 'request': 11}, 'logger_stats': {'id': 'logger_stats', 'content': \"logger.py: NewLineFormatter.__init__(fmt, datefmt=None, high_precision=False, use_color=False) stores flags. format() calls super().format(record) producing full string with prefix and message; then adds prefix after newlines (record.message), applies color. To add budget: add keyword-only max_message_chars after 4 positional params, validate >=32 and not bool, save budget. In format(), truncate record.message portion before multi-line handling - must not mutate record.msg/args. _setup_logger creates handler once, always resets formatter with NewLineFormatter(_FORMAT, datefmt, use_color) - add max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS there. init_logger attaches _default_handler if not already present. stats_logger._log_worker iterates queue batches, calls logger.info(m) per message; change to logger.info(m, extra={'keep_full_message': True}).\", 'sources': ['deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py', 'deepinfer/logger.py'], 'evidence_ids': ['ev-30754515034e43628968', 'ev-51e2fa3b9fc1aebe86f3', 'ev-5a3c8c1ca1246b61b813', 'ev-5abfdabfb975754c668